As someone who's neither a newbie nor an expert, what I find
most helpful here is people giving different advice while explaining
their rationales and styles of play, so I can evaluate the advice
for myself and decide whether it's a good idea and fits the way
I like to play (not the same thing). For instance, when James
said he played as a near-pacifist, I knew that I wouldn't value
scrolls of scare monster as much as he does. But his point
about crumbling scrolls if you pick them up is useful anyway.

The one-upmanship is not so helpful.


